{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Circle","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.faddeev_modular_parameter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.faddeev_modular_parameter","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EllipticRTheta.lean#L100-L112","doc":"**The Faddeev elliptic modular parameter is `τ = 1/b²`.** The elliptic freedom\n(`FaddeevPhiEllipticFreedom.faddeevPhi_mul_elliptic`) lives on the period lattice\n`⟨ib, i/b⟩`; the modular parameter of that lattice is the period ratio\n`τ = ω₂/ω₁ = (i/b)/(ib) = 1/b²`. So the single modular parameter of\n`SingleTauChannelClosure` is **substrate-derived** — a fixed function `τ = 1/b²`\nof the Faddeev modulus `b`, **not** a free fit. This is the concrete object whose\n(archimedean) evaluation the `c₃` cross-anchor swing would have to track; it turns\nthe \"single `τ`\" from an abstract hypothesis into a computable prediction. The\nmodular double `b ↔ 1/b` sends `τ = 1/b² ↦ b² = 1/τ` — the `S`-transform, the\ntheta-modular symmetry that mixes the θ-even/θ-odd (bar-even/bar-odd) sectors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.channels_locked","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.channels_locked","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EllipticRTheta.lean#L88-L98","doc":"**Consequence of single-`τ` closure: the two channels are functionally\ndependent.** If both factor through one `τ`, then equal `τ`-values force equal\nchannel-values — the bar-odd and bar-even readings are locked together, never\nindependently tunable. (A trivial but honest consequence, exhibiting that the\nclass asserts real joint content.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.SingleTauChannelClosure.tau_nonconstant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.SingleTauChannelClosure.tau_nonconstant","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EllipticRTheta.lean#L86-L86","doc":"`τ` genuinely varies across anchors (the `c₃` swing is not degenerate). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.SingleTauChannelClosure.even_factors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.SingleTauChannelClosure.even_factors","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EllipticRTheta.lean#L84-L84","doc":"the bar-even channel factors through the **same** `τ` (the non-independence). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.SingleTauChannelClosure.odd_factors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.SingleTauChannelClosure.odd_factors","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EllipticRTheta.lean#L82-L82","doc":"the bar-odd channel factors through the single modular parameter `τ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.SingleTauChannelClosure.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.SingleTauChannelClosure.mk","kind":"ctor","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EllipticRTheta.lean#L80-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.SingleTauChannelClosure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.SingleTauChannelClosure","kind":"class","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EllipticRTheta.lean#L70-L86","doc":"**Single-`τ` non-independence (conjecture, §3b).** The bar-odd channel\n`barOdd(a)` (the `c₃`/`Q_β` swing across substrate anchors `a`) and the bar-even\nchannel `barEven(a)` (the mass/binding correction) both **factor through one**\nelliptic modular parameter `τ(a)`: there are fixed profiles `f, g` (the\nθ-even/θ-odd quotients of the elliptic `R`) with `barOdd = f ∘ τ` and\n`barEven = g ∘ τ`. The content is the **shared** `τ`: the `(barOdd, barEven)`\ntrajectory is a **1-parameter curve**, not a 2-D independent pair — the\nnon-independence the transfer matrix encodes. `tau_nonconstant` records that the\nswing is real (the parameter genuinely varies across anchors), so the closure is\nnon-degenerate. No instance is provided: this is the open hypothesis to test. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.qexp_barSplit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.qexp_barSplit","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EllipticRTheta.lean#L63-L68","doc":"**Exact even/odd split of the `q`-exponential** (`eᵘ = cosh u + sinh u`): the\nbar-even and bar-odd parts are the θ-even and θ-odd sectors, and their sum is the\nfull (elliptic-liftable) object. The transfer-matrix mixing of the two sectors is\nprecisely the failure of this split to be preserved by the elliptic `R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.sinh_barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.sinh_barOdd","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EllipticRTheta.lean#L60-L61","doc":"`sinh` is **bar-odd** under `u ↦ −u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.cosh_barEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.cosh_barEven","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EllipticRTheta.lean#L56-L58","doc":"`cosh` is **bar-even** under `u ↦ −u` (the parity the elliptic transfer matrix\nmixes with the odd sector). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.barOdd_hecke_eq_two_sinh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.barOdd_hecke_eq_two_sinh","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EllipticRTheta.lean#L49-L54","doc":"**Bar-odd Hecke combination = `2 sinh`.** The antisymmetric `q − q⁻¹` (the\nskein relation, the `Q_β`/`c₃` channel) is `2 sinh u` — the degeneration of the\nodd theta `θ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.barEven_hecke_eq_two_cosh","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EllipticRTheta.barEven_hecke_eq_two_cosh","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EllipticRTheta.lean#L42-L47","doc":"**Bar-even Hecke combination = `2 cosh`.** For `q = eᵘ`, the symmetric Hecke\neigenvalue sum `q + q⁻¹` is `2 cosh u` — the trigonometric degeneration of the\neven Jacobi theta `θ_even`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}